{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9eb-d8c0-74d1-b394-64cb248a951b"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"a3fdabb1-ccbe-4a5e-91a4-121d521ff754","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"a3fdabb1-ccbe-4a5e-91a4-121d521ff754","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a3fdabb1-ccbe-4a5e-91a4-121d521ff754"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(BUG-260916-2764p8, status=development)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `developer` (`implementer`) — Writes code, fixes bugs, writes tests\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `swiftui`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/swiftui/SKILL.md`\n- `core-data`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/core-data/SKILL.md`\n- `go-testing-tools`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Diagnose the actual Swift6.1 weak declaration compiler error and make the minimal semantics-preserving correction, using existing ownership/release tests where sufficient.\n- [ ] Verify exact accepted PR6 prerequisite bytes separately from the new delta and run appropriate focused checks; record toolchain/SDK and real-hosted-proof bounds honestly.\n- [ ] Attach exact candidate, validation evidence and prospective composition boundary for independent review; no publication, managed-branch commit, new unrelated fix or VPN operation.\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** BUG-260916-2764p8\n- **Title:** BUG-260916-2764p8: fix-swift61-m1-runtime-weak-capture-compilation\n- **Parent:** STORY-260916-1du4i1\n\n### Description\n\nHosted CI run35087910852 on signed PR6 head310a560916d8b8012fa238f65b51649041caee4d now compiles MacOSSSHBootstrapErrorMapper but fails in Sources/ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport/M1RuntimeCommand.swift:138:16: weak must be a mutable variable, because it may change at runtime. Diagnose and minimally fix Swift6.1 compatibility while preserving runtime ownership, cancellation and weak-reference behavior. File belongs to accepted but unlanded Shared Runtime PR stack, not fresh remote main. Reuse accepted prerequisite bytes with exact identity evidence; no unrelated repairs.\n\n### Scope\n\nMinimal harness compatibility source/test delta on the verified accepted PR6 composition. Managed candidate may include only exact accepted prerequisite stack bytes needed to validate this unlanded source; identify them separately from new delta. No gate relaxation, tooling edits, VPN operations, routing changes or publication before independent review.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nWeak-reference semantics and runtime ownership remain correct; focused meaningful validation passes with exact toolchain bounds recorded; accepted prerequisite identities and new delta are independently reviewable. Hosted Swift6.1 proof and exact signed-head review are subsequent delivery gates, not producer handoff prerequisites.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### BUG-260916-2764p8_implementation-brief.md\n> Minimal weak-declaration repair on accepted PR prerequisite stack\n\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.temp/resources/BUG-260916-2764p8/BUG-260916-2764p8_implementation-brief.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2602`\n- Content digest: `sha256:fff15df4abad2f2dcb0f019328a463163459bd4de62406177cdb9c965c097c78`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### BUG-260916-2764p8_toolchain-bound.md\n> Correct evidence bound from publication outcome\n\nCorrection to earlier shorthand Swift6.1: TASK-260916-235lb7_results.md reports the fresh run35087910852 SwiftPM failure log has no actual Xcode/Swift version strings, and workflow uses macos-15 without a pin. Do NOT assert a specific compiler version from this job alone. weak let is a language-level diagnostic, potentially reproducible on current local compiler too; reproduce against the full real PR6 harness composition rather than old-main target subset. Exact failure is unchanged: M1RuntimeCommand.swift:138:16 weak must be a mutable variable. Source and prior run evidence must be distinguished. Publication result and 685-line job log are now attached under TASK-260916-235lb7. Source-review on an old-main subset did not compile this PR-only file; full composed candidate validation is required for the new repair. Avoid building mock substitutes. Preserve weak lifetime semantics and demonstrate existing owner release/cleanup assertions through the real harness.\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `BUG-260916-2764p8_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(BUG-260916-2764p8, name=BUG-260916-2764p8_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff BUG-260916-2764p8 --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260916-1du4i1.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260916-1du4i1/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260916-1du4i1`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n"}}
