{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cadd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9eb-d8c0-74d1-b394-64cb248a951b"},"sequence":969,"recorded_at":1780531400001933,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a3fdabb1-ccbe-4a5e-91a4-121d521ff754","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a3fdabb1-ccbe-4a5e-91a4-121d521ff754","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a3fdabb1-ccbe-4a5e-91a4-121d521ff754"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a9f0-74f4-7702-8ae8-6f2c57f90aca"},"task_id":"01a0a9f0-74f4-7702-8ae8-6f2c57f90aca","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a9f0-74f4-7702-8ae8-6f2c57f90aca","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-42-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'add_resource(BUG-260916-2764p8, name=BUG-260916-2764p8_results.md, type=outcome, description=\\\"Handoff evidence: weak-var repair on PR6 composition\\\", content=\\\"# BUG-260916-2764p8 results: weak-capture compilation repair\\\\n\\\\n## Diagnosis\\\\nHosted run35087910852 failed at Sources/ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport/M1RuntimeCommand.swift:138:16 with `weak must be a mutable variable`.\\\\nRoot cause: line 138 declared `weak let weakHostOwner = hostOwner`. Older Swift (hosted macos-15 CI toolchain) rejects `weak let`\\\\nas a language-level error; `weak` references must be `var` because ARC zeroes them at runtime. The declaration feeds the\\\\nrelease check at lines 169-173 (`hostOwner = nil; guard weakHostOwner == nil else { throw hostLifetimeInvariant }`).\\\\nOnly occurrence of `weak let` in Sources/ and Tests/ (regex search) — no sibling sites.\\\\n\\\\n## Fix (1 line, semantics-preserving)\\\\n```diff\\\\n-      weak let weakHostOwner = hostOwner\\\\n+      weak var weakHostOwner = hostOwner\\\\n```\\\\nFile: Sources/ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport/M1RuntimeCommand.swift:138. No behavior change: same ARC-zeroed weak optional,\\\\nsame nil-check, same hostLifetimeInvariant gate, same cancellation/ownership flow. No new tests: brief directs reuse of\\\\nexisting M1 ownership/release suites; a compiler-spelling fix has no new behavior to cover.\\\\n\\\\n## Prerequisite stack identity (reused bytes, NOT new scope)\\\\n- PR6 head: 310a560916d8b8012fa238f65b51649041caee4d (verified via rev-parse; also origin/delivery/STORY-260715-1y04r0-rev3)\\\\n- Worktree HEAD (unmoved): b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74 on task-board/story/STORY-260916-1du4i1, nothing committed\\\\n- Overlay: all tracked non-board paths checked out from PR6 head; staged diff stat exactly matches\\\\n  `git diff b3422b0..310a560` (59 files, 8970 insertions, 65 deletions)\\\\n- Pre-fix file blob == PR6 blob: bcd896110682117e347fda955c9024e71297e9cf (exact identity)\\\\n- Post-fix file blob: d868eb7be3849c8aa0da84a0423de6c5476ebb38\\\\n- New delta vs PR6 head (`git diff 310a560 --stat`): 1 file, 1 insertion, 1 deletion (the line above)\\\\n- Candidate layout: staged = prerequisite overlay; unstaged = new delta only; .task-board artifact untouched; no untracked files\\\\n\\\\n## Validation (all on full composed candidate, real code, exit codes observed)\\\\n- `swift build --target ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport` (pre-fix, PR6 bytes): exit 0 — local Swift 6.3.2 ACCEPTS `weak let`,\\\\n  so the hosted failure is NOT reproducible on this toolchain (see bound below). Minimal swiftc -typecheck probe confirms.\\\\n- `swift build --target ReluxTunnelHarnessSupport` (post-fix): exit 0, one benign warning:\\\\n  `#WeakMutability: weak variable was never mutated; consider let` — new-toolchain-only diagnostic; no warnings-as-errors\\\\n  in Package.swift; `weak var` is the unique spelling compiling on both old (hosted) and new (local) Swift.\\\\n- `swift build` (all targets): exit 0\\\\n- `swift test --filter M1RuntimeHarnessTests|DeterministicSessionFactory`: 9 tests, 2 suites, pass, exit 0\\\\n- `swift test --filter MacOSProductionRuntimeOwnership|M1RuntimeComposition`: 11 tests, 2 suites, pass, exit 0\\\\n- Combined post-restore re-run: 20 tests, 4 suites, pass, exit 0\\\\n- Real binary end-to-end: `swift build --product ReluxTunnelHarness` exit 0, then\\\\n  `python3 scripts/validate-m1-runtime-harness.py --executable .build/debug/ReluxTunnelHarness`: passed=True, 7/7 fixtures, exit 0\\\\n  (validator asserts zero `harness.m1.host_owner_retained` gauge through the fixed production path)\\\\n- Narrowing mutant (weak->strong `var weakHostOwner`, gate stays present): `swift test --filter M1RuntimeHarnessTests`\\\\n  FAILS, 6 tests, 14 issues, exit 1 (hostLifetimeInvariant fires, exit .failure) — proves the suite guards weak semantics;\\\\n  mutant reverted, green re-observed after restore (20/20 above)\\\\n- Lint: no linter configured in repo (no lint target in Makefile/CI); only diagnostic is the known benign #WeakMutability warning\\\\n\\\\n## AC coverage: 4 of 4 rows driven through production entry\\\\nProduction call site: HarnessApplication.run([m1-runtime,...]) -> M1RuntimeHarnessCommand.run (M1RuntimeCommand.swift:118).\\\\n1. Weak-reference semantics correct: productionEntryDoesNotRetainOrConsultHostOwner + successfulComposedGenerations\\\\n   assert exit .success and host_owner_retained==0 through the production entry; mutant proves sensitivity.\\\\n2. Runtime ownership correct: macOS production runtime ownership suite + M1 runtime composition suite (11 tests) pass.\\\\n3. Focused validation passes + toolchain bounds recorded: this document; see bound below.\\\\n4. Prerequisite identities + new delta independently reviewable: identities and 1-line diff above; candidate uncommitted.\\\\n\\\\n## Toolchain / proof bounds (honest)\\\\n- Local: Apple Swift 6.3.2 (swiftlang-6.3.2.1.108 clang-2100.1.1.101), Xcode 26.5 (17F42), macOS 27.0 host,\\\\n  target arm64-apple-macosx28.0. Per toolchain-bound note, NO compiler version is asserted for hosted run35087910852\\\\n  (macos-15, unpinned, log has no version strings).\\\\n- Local toolchain accepts BOTH spellings, so this run proves the repair compiles and behaves correctly on Swift 6.3.2\\\\n  but cannot reproduce the original hosted error; hosted proof on the older toolchain remains a subsequent delivery gate\\\\n  (accepted per task AC, not a producer handoff prerequisite).\\\\n- Full credential-free/xcodebuild gate not run locally (requires legacy relux-proxy root + generated workspace); SwiftPM\\\\n  build/test + real-binary fixture validation is the focused bound.\\\\n\\\\n## Prospective composition boundary\\\\nUncommitted candidate = exact PR6 prerequisite bytes (staged, 59 files) + 1-line weak-var delta (unstaged).\\\\nIndependent review: verify staged tree equals PR6 head minus .task-board, then review the single unstaged hunk.\\\\nNo publication, branch commit, VPN operation, routing change, or unrelated fix performed.\\\\n\\\")' 2>&1 | head -n 10\",\n  \"description\": \"Attach outcome evidence to board\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"BUG-260916-2764p8\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"BUG-260916-2764p8_results.md\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"outcome\\\",\\\"uri\\\":\\\"file://BUG-260916-2764p8/BUG-260916-2764p8_results.md\\\"}}\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 165,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 42,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
